course: dictionary
lesson: 12491
title: Denial: saying no to the truth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A denial is when someone says that something is not true. Look at the words around it for clues. «The shop owner gave a firm denial that the milk had gone off.» The owner is saying, "No, that is not true," so a denial is a statement that something is not true.
explain: Denial can also mean refusing to give someone something. «The judge's denial of the family's appeal meant they could not stay in their home.» The judge said no, so denial here means refusing.
explain: Someone who is «in denial» will not accept a painful truth. «Sam was in denial about his dog being ill, and kept saying it would be fine.» Sam knows the truth hurts, so he pretends it is not real.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Can you put "refusal" or "no" in place of denial and still make sense? If yes, you have the right meaning.
fact: Denial is a noun, and its plural is denials.
fact: «Denial» means saying that something is not true.
fact: «Denial» can also mean refusing to give someone something, as in «denial of rights».
fact: Being «in denial» means not accepting a painful truth.
fact: In the Easter story, Peter's denial was when he said he did not know Jesus.
exercise: «Jay says his team did not lose, even though the scoreboard shows it.» Jay is in denial. What does in denial mean? | Being very tired after the game | *Not accepting a painful truth | Feeling happy about the score | Counting the points carefully
exercise: «The shop owner issued a denial that the milk had gone off.» What is a denial here? | Running out of the shop | Giving a free gift to customers | Painting the shop door | *Saying that something is not true
exercise: «The guard's denial of entry stopped the children from getting in.» What does denial mean here? | Asking for their names | *Refusing to let them in | Waving hello | Letting them in for free
test: «Ben said he did not break the window, and his denial was firm.» What is Ben's denial? | Fixing the window | Breaking the window again | Telling a joke | *Saying it is not true that he broke it
test: What does «in denial» mean in «Mia was in denial about losing her cat»? | Being very loud | Looking for her cat | *Not accepting that she had lost her cat | Feeling proud of her cat
exam: In the Easter story, what was Peter's denial? | Saying he could fly | *Saying he did not know Jesus | Saying he had lost his coat | Saying he would sail the sea
